in @glass

# Property: for every shard at depth >= 1 under `@epistemologic`, the
# first path segment AFTER `@epistemologic` must equal the declaration
# keyword used inside the file.
#
# Self-witnessing: this property's own shard MUST live at
# `@epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_path_root` and declare with
# `pact`. It satisfies its own check on the first frame. The RED's
# `does_NOT_live_under_epistemologic_property` assertion enforces
# this.
#
# === Recognition shape ===
#
# Recognition #37 (`requires` IS a Paskian agreement; promoted
# 2026-06-10) named `pact` as the property-declaration form. `pact`
# replaced the conversation-era `grammar` keyword as the surface
# for declaring properties. Every property shard since then
# declares with `pact` inside the body. The path segment
# `property` is the residue that didn't move with the keyword.
# The substrate already had the word
# ([[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]); this property
# names the rule that aligns the path to it.
#
# === Operational discharge ===
#
# Mara's cross-shard resolver (mirror commit `128e0d2`, the @io
# floor that walks `shards/` + `boot/std/` and builds the
# declared-namespace index spanning the whole corpus) makes the
# keyword/path-root check tractable to discharge today: the
# realisation layer projects the declared namespace and the
# declaration keyword off the same single source of record (the
# shard file's first concrete top-level declaration), no further
# pipeline work required.
#
# === Migration intent ===
#
# Seven existing property shards landed under `@epistemologic/property/`
# before this rule was named (recognition #37 promoted `pact` but the
# path segment didn't move). They migrate to `@epistemologic/pact/`
# under this property's gaze:
#
#   @epistemologic/property/path_matches_namespace
#     -> @epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace
#   @epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth
#     -> @epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_depth
#   @epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic
#     -> @epistemologic/pact/parent_acyclic
#   @epistemologic/property/symbol_canonical_form
#     -> @epistemologic/pact/symbol_canonical_form
#   @epistemologic/property/gate_matches_diff_closure
#     -> @epistemologic/pact/gate_matches_diff_closure
#   @epistemologic/property/dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth
#     -> @epistemologic/pact/dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth
#   @epistemologic/property/operator_matches_composition_primitive
#     -> @epistemologic/pact/operator_matches_composition_primitive
#
# Each migration is one `git mv` plus an in-file rewrite of
# `pact @epistemologic/property/<X>` -> `pact @epistemologic/pact/<X>`
# and `out @epistemologic/property/<X>` -> `out @epistemologic/pact/<X>`.
# The 6 fracture-shard `in @epistemologic/property/<X>` imports in
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/` move in lockstep.
#
# === Path-root extraction ===
#
# For a declared namespace `@epistemologic/<root>/<rest>`, the
# `path_root` is the first segment after `@epistemologic` (here,
# `<root>`). For `@epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_path_root`,
# path_root = `pact`. For the dark shards still under
# `@epistemologic/property/<X>`, path_root = `property`.
#
# === Declaration keyword ===
#
# `declaration_keyword` projects the keyword used in the file's
# first concrete top-level declaration of the namespace. For
# `pact @epistemologic/<root>/<rest> { ... }`, the keyword is
# `pact`. The substrate's keyword inventory at depth >= 1 (per
# @epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_depth post-migration) is
# `glass | pact | <optical>`; the rule below ranges over `pact`
# specifically, since `pact` is the only keyword whose path-root
# segment must match (the optical schematic elements live under
# `@optics/...`, not `@epistemologic/...`; `glass` lives at the
# substrate root).
#
# === Verdict surface ===
#
# Verdict surface is transparency<p>:
#   success              -- the declaration keyword equals the
#                          first path segment after `@epistemologic`
#                          (today: `pact` matches `pact`).
#   failure(opacity_map) -- the declaration keyword disagrees with
#                          the path root (today: `pact` declared
#                          under `@epistemologic/property/<X>` is
#                          one opacity per offending shard file).
#   partial(opacity_map) -- multiple concrete top-level @<X>
#                          declarations, some match and some don't.
#
# Located transparency (not @glass.verdict): the kintsugi loop
# consumes the opacity_map to direct migration. Each opacity in
# the failure map names ONE offending shard file; the fracture
# body (forward-promised sibling tick under `@kintsugi/fracture/`)
# emits the morphism that proposes `git mv` of the offending shard
# plus the in-file `pact @<old> -> pact @<new>` rewrite, plus the
# `in @<old> -> in @<new>` sweep across consumers. The property
# names the rule; the fracture realises it; the kintsugi loop is
# the bridge.
#
# === Form-side discipline ===
#
# This property sits at the form-side of the form/process partition
# ([[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]; the
# @mirror = form, @kintsugi = process partition). The rule names
# WHAT must hold at the keyword/path-root altitude; the
# realisation lives in @kintsugi/fracture/<sibling>; the operator
# of the bridge is the kintsugi loop (substrate-pull).

pact @epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_path_root {
  # The path root of a file's declared namespace: the first
  # segment after `@epistemologic`. For
  # `@epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_path_root` this is
  # `pact`. For a shard still declaring under
  # `@epistemologic/property/<X>` this is `property`.
  #
  # Multiple concrete top-level declarations yield one entry per
  # declaration in declaration order.
  path_root(file: ref) -> text { \ }

  # The declaration keyword each concrete top-level @<name>
  # declaration uses in `file`. One entry per declared namespace
  # in declaration order, parallel to `path_root`. Entries are
  # one of `prism | glass | pact | facet | stage | aperture |
  # splitter | resonator | bench | source | detector` per
  # @epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_depth's keyword
  # inventory.
  declaration_keyword(file: ref) -> text { \ }

  # The combined property: for every concrete top-level
  # declaration `<keyword> @epistemologic/<root>/<rest> { ... }`
  # in `file`, `<keyword>` equals `<root>`.
  #
  # Today the rule names `pact` specifically — `pact` is the
  # only declaration keyword whose namespace lives under
  # `@epistemologic/<keyword>/...`. The other keywords from the
  # depth>=1 inventory (`glass`, the optical schematics) declare
  # under other family roots (`@glass`, `@optics/...`); the rule
  # is vacuously satisfied at those declaration sites.
  #
  # Verdict surface is transparency<p>:
  #   success              -- declaration_keyword equals path_root
  #                          for every concrete top-level
  #                          declaration in `file`.
  #   failure(opacity_map) -- some declaration's keyword
  #                          disagrees with its path root; each
  #                          opacity names ONE offending shard
  #                          file plus the (keyword, path_root)
  #                          pair that disagrees.
  #   partial(opacity_map) -- multiple concrete top-level
  #                          declarations, mixed verdict.
  keyword_matches_path_root(file: ref) -> transparency { \ }
}

out path_root
out declaration_keyword
out keyword_matches_path_root
out @epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_path_root
